# fixedbugs, M-c-callbacks step 0, 2026-09-05 (panel 111 R4).
#
# THE SECOND SHAPE OF `ffi_callback_type`, and it is here because the provoking
# case is a witness and not the class (CLAUDE.md §1). Its sibling
# `ffi-callback-signature-the-header-refutes.hero` is a callback whose ARITY and
# parameter type disagree with the header. This one agrees on both and still does
# not bind, because the header qualifies what the pointers point at.
#
# SYMPTOM: `selfhost/emit/ctype.hero` promised in writing that "a Heroes function
# value and a C callback are the same eight bytes, which is what makes qsort and
# every raylib callback expressible". Measured the day the permission landed, the
# promise is false: `stdlib.h` declares the comparator
# `int (*)(const void *, const void *)`, Heroes emits `int (*)(void *, void *)`,
# and clang refuses the two as incompatible function pointer types.
#
# CAUSE: THE LANGUAGE, not the emitter. There is no spelling for a const pointee
# at all — `cstr` is `const char *`, `ptr` is `void *`, and there is no third. So
# this is not a defect with a fix in this file; it is a hole with a diagnostic,
# and the diagnostic's second note names it as one.
#
# WHAT IS OWED: `docs/work/SCHEDULED.md` carries the sitting, at this milestone.
# Panel 111 R4 left two routes — the `c_int`/`const` vocabulary, or a design.md
# Part 8 wart with its return condition — and both are language changes. Until
# one lands, this case is what keeps the refusal honest: it fires, it lands on
# the author's own line at exit 1, and it says what cannot be written rather than
# letting clang blame the compiler at exit 2.

extern "stdlib.h"
    function qsort(base: ptr, n: u64, size: u64, compar: (function(left: ptr, right: ptr) -> i32))  #~ ffi_callback_type

# The two pointers are named since defect 026: `compar`'s type has two `ptr`,
# so it names them, and a function handed to it declares the same two names.
# They are discarded rather than read, because what this case is about is the
# const pointee and a comparator that compared would say nothing more about it.
function cmp(left: ptr, right: ptr) -> i32
    _ = left
    _ = right
    return 0

function main()
    qsort(nullptr, n: 0, size: 0, cmp)
